# RTK - Rust Token Killer

RTK compresses command outputs (typically 60–90% fewer tokens).
Installed at `/Users/mnemonic/.local/bin/rtk`.

## Mandatory rule

**When using the Shell tool, prefix the following diagnostic commands
with `rtk`.**

Do **not** use `rtk` for state-changing commands (write, create, install,
commit, push) — only for read / diagnostic commands.

## Commands to rewrite

### Git
| Instead of | Use |
|---|---|
| `git status` | `rtk git status` |
| `git diff ...` | `rtk git diff ...` |
| `git log ...` | `rtk git log ...` |
| `git show ...` | `rtk git show ...` |
| `git branch ...` | `rtk git branch ...` |

### Files and search
| Instead of | Use |
|---|---|
| `cat <file>` | `rtk read <file>` |
| `grep` / `rg <pattern>` | `rtk grep <pattern>` |
| `find <path> ...` | `rtk find <path> ...` |
| `ls ...` | `rtk ls ...` |
| `tree ...` | `rtk tree ...` |
| `diff <a> <b>` | `rtk diff <a> <b>` |
| `head -N <file>` | `rtk read <file> --max-lines N` |

### GitHub CLI
| Instead of | Use |
|---|---|
| `gh pr ...` | `rtk gh pr ...` |
| `gh issue ...` | `rtk gh issue ...` |
| `gh run ...` | `rtk gh run ...` |
| `gh api ...` | `rtk gh api ...` |

### Containers / network
| Instead of | Use |
|---|---|
| `docker ps/images/logs/build` | `rtk docker …` |
| `docker compose ps/logs/build` | `rtk docker compose …` |
| `curl ...` / `wget ...` | `rtk curl …` / `rtk wget …` |

### Rust / Topcoat (when present)

Use the host `cargo` / `rustc`. Do **not** force `rustup run` or
`cargo +<toolchain>` unless the user asks.

| Instead of | Use |
|---|---|
| `cargo test …` | `rtk cargo test … -- --test-threads=1` |
| `cargo clippy …` | `rtk cargo clippy … --all-targets -- -D warnings` |
| `cargo fmt …` | `rtk cargo fmt …` |
| `cargo check\|build …` | `rtk cargo check\|build …` |
| `topcoat fmt …` | run as needed (state-changing format: no `rtk` required) |

Hand-off validation is **clippy + tests**, not `cargo check` alone.
See `dev-validation-cycle.mdc` and the `quality-assurance` skill.

### Other diagnostics

- `rtk npm test|run …` / `rtk pnpm …` / `rtk yarn …` if ever present
- `rtk kubectl get|logs|describe …` when debugging deployed envs

## Exceptions — do NOT prefix with rtk

- Commands already prefixed with `rtk`
- Commands with heredocs (`<<`)
- `git commit`, `git push`, `git add`
- Actual installs (`npm install`, `cargo install`, …)
- Complex pipes (`cmd1 | cmd2`) unless the first command is simple
- Interactive commands
